# Strict Typing & ESLint Standards

### ❌ NEVER use `any` to bypass type errors
Use proper interfaces, types, or type guards.

### ❌ NEVER turn off warnings or errors in eslint config or disable inline
When asked to fix linting or type-checking issues, fix the actual code and types.

### ❌ NEVER automatically run `pnpm run type`, `tsc`, `pnpm run lint`, or `eslint`
Leave type-checking and linting to the user (unless explicitly requested).
